mov: an interrupt in a fragment's sample is no lost or cut sample

When the caller's interrupt callback stops a read of the input (with
0099, hls reads a segment on after it), mov_read_packet() lost samples:
av_get_packet() returned the part of the sample that was read, flagged
corrupt, and mov handed it on (the decoder got a cut access unit); on the
next call the seek to the next sample failed on the latched error, the
sample was skipped as a partial file, and so was the one after it while
the read was not yet flowing again. One interrupt in a fragmented MP4
segment (fMP4/CMAF HLS) gave a corrupt access unit and two lost ones:
artefacts until the next keyframe. A player that interrupts the read
while paused (to stop prefetching) met it on every long pause.

When the seek to a sample fails and the input's error is AVERROR_EXIT
(the last read ended in the interrupt), give the sample back and return
AVERROR_EXIT: it is asked for again on the next call. When a sample's
read comes back short with that error, drop what was read and seek back
to the sample's start; the seek is within the I/O buffer when it still
holds the sample's start, and the sample is read again on the next call.
Else (a sample larger than the buffer, or one that spanned a refill) it
is lost, but not handed on cut. A stale AVERROR_EXIT in the error of an
input that is not hls already ends avio_read(), so other callers see no
change. Only the plain sample read: the EIA-608, APV and IAMF reads
are left as they are.

diff --git a/libavformat/mov.c b/libavformat/mov.c
--- a/libavformat/mov.c
+++ b/libavformat/mov.c
@@ -11498,6 +11498,13 @@ static int mov_read_packet(AVFormatContext *s, AVPacket *pkt)
     if (st->discard != AVDISCARD_ALL || sc->iamf) {
         int64_t ret64 = avio_seek(sc->pb, sample->pos, SEEK_SET);
         if (ret64 != sample->pos) {
+            /* The caller's interrupt callback cut the last read (its
+             * AVERROR_EXIT is latched in the I/O context): the sample is
+             * asked for again on the next call. */
+            if (sc->pb->error == AVERROR_EXIT) {
+                mov_current_sample_dec(sc);
+                return AVERROR_EXIT;
+            }
             av_log(mov->fc, AV_LOG_ERROR, "stream %d, offset 0x%"PRIx64": partial file\n",
                    sc->ffindex, sample->pos);
             if (should_retry(sc->pb, ret64)) {
@@ -11555,8 +11562,18 @@ static int mov_read_packet(AVFormatContext *s, AVPacket *pkt)
                 return AVERROR_INVALIDDATA;
             }
             ret = av_get_packet(sc->pb, pkt, au_size);
-        } else
+        } else {
             ret = av_get_packet(sc->pb, pkt, sample->size);
+            if (ret >= 0 && ret < sample->size && sc->pb->error == AVERROR_EXIT) {
+                /* The interrupt cut the sample. Back to its start when the
+                 * buffer still holds it (an in-buffer seek: it is read again
+                 * on the next call); else it is lost, but not handed on cut. */
+                av_packet_unref(pkt);
+                if (avio_seek(sc->pb, sample->pos, SEEK_SET) == sample->pos)
+                    mov_current_sample_dec(sc);
+                return AVERROR_EXIT;
+            }
+        }
         if (ret < 0) {
             if (should_retry(sc->pb, ret)) {
                 mov_current_sample_dec(sc);
